# Every change needs @bozmund's approval before it can merge.
#
# The `Protect main` ruleset already sets `require_code_owner_review: true`,
# but that rule is inert without this file — with no owners defined there is no
# code-owner review to require, so any collaborator's approval satisfied it.
#
# This is also what makes auto-merge safe to leave enabled repository-wide.
# GitHub has no per-user auto-merge permission: anyone with write access can
# turn it on. Auto-merge does not skip reviews though — it waits for them — so
# gating the review here means nothing reaches main without @bozmund, whoever
# queued it.
* @bozmund
